{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.MesonQcgFusionIdentity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.MesonQcgFusionIdentity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.meson_qCG_3x4_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.meson_qCG_3x4_classical","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/meson-qcg-fusion-identity.lean#L59-L62","doc":"Decategorified form: at `q = 1` the q-Clebsch–Gordan reduces to the\nclassical SU(2) dimension identity `3 · 4 = 2 + 4 + 6` (the classical\nlimit observed in `meson_3x4_structural_origin.py`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.meson_qCG_3x4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.meson_qCG_3x4","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/meson-qcg-fusion-identity.lean#L33-L57","doc":"q-Clebsch–Gordan fusion in the **multiplied-through** form: clearing\nthe denominator `(q − q⁻¹)` from `[3]_q · [4]_q = [2]_q + [4]_q + [6]_q`\nyields a ring identity. This is the math-exact derived piece behind the\nmeson GMOR fusion `m_K²/m_π² = [3]_q · [4]_q`.\n\nBase ring (AGENTS.md §7c): stated over a bare `CommRing` with the inverse\ncarried as the companion variable `qi` subject to the unit relation\n`q · qi = 1` — the division-free `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` form the module docstring\nabove describes.  A field instance is recovered by taking `qi = q⁻¹` and\n`hq = mul_inv_cancel₀`.  The difference of the two sides factors through\nthe unit relation, so the proof is one `ring` identity plus `hq`; no\n`field_simp`, no inverse. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:meson-qcg-fusion-identity","label":"prop:meson-qcg-fusion-identity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/meson-qcg-fusion-identity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}